$\Class{W}[2]\not\subseteq \Para\Class{AC}^{0}$, and, hence, a
$\Class{W}[2]$-hard problem cannot lie in $\Para\Class{AC}^{0}$. It is furthermore widely conjectured
that $\Class{W}[2]\not\subseteq \Para\Class{AC}^{0\uparrow}$, as
$\Para\Class{AC}^{0\uparrow}\subseteq \Class{FPT}$. We devote the rest of
this section to proving the individual items of the lemma.

