1748-<div id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29" class="ltx_para">
1749-<p id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Forward direction.</em>
1750-Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(S\mathbin{\dot{\cup}}U,\adj,k)\in\mathrm{p}\text{{-set-cover}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>∪</mo><mo>˙</mo></mover><mi>U</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">-set-cover</mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(S\mathbin{\dot{\cup}}U,\adj,k)\in\mathrm{p}\text{{-set-cover}}</annotation></semantics></math> be given. We need
1751:to show that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(G^{\prime},k^{\prime})\in\mathrm{p\text{-}}\mathchoice{\text{\small$\mathrm{VD}$}}{\text{\small$\mathrm{VD}$}}{\text{$\mathrm{VD}$}}{\text{$\mathrm{VD}$}}_{\mathrm{basic}}(\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mtext>-</mtext><mi mathsize="0.900em">VD</mi></mrow><mi>basic</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2" title="Lower Bounds ‣ 3 Basic Graphs ‣ On the Descriptive Complexity of Vertex Deletion Problems" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(G^{\prime},k^{\prime})\in\mathrm{p\text{-}}\mathchoice{\text{\small$\mathrm{VD}$}}{\text{\small$\mathrm{VD}$}}{\text{$\mathrm{VD}$}}{\text{$\mathrm{VD}$}}_{\mathrm{basic}}(\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}})</annotation></semantics></math> holds. Let <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subseteq S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subseteq S</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C|\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C|\leq k</annotation></semantics></math> cover <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>. We claim that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}\setminus C\models\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>⊧</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2" title="Lower Bounds ‣ 3 Basic Graphs ‣ On the Descriptive Complexity of Vertex Deletion Problems" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}\setminus C\models\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}}</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, removing
1752-all <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in C</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> destroys all triangles that could violate
1753:<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2" title="Lower Bounds ‣ 3 Basic Graphs ‣ On the Descriptive Complexity of Vertex Deletion Problems" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us go over the different
1754-vertices still left in <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p29.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\prime}\setminus C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\prime}\setminus C</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
1755-</div>
1756:<div id="Thmtheorem13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
1757:<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 13</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
1758:<div id="Thmtheorem13.p1" class="ltx_para">
1759:<p id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For all <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, each vertices <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s,s^{\prime},s^{\prime\prime},s^{\prime\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s,s^{\prime},s^{\prime\prime},s^{\prime\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> has an incident
1760:edge in <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> that is not part of a triangle. This still holds for
1761:<math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime},s^{\prime\prime},s^{\prime\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′′′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime},s^{\prime\prime},s^{\prime\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}\setminus C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}\setminus C</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem13.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in C</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, for the
