1798:Conversely, suppose that for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}=(V^{\prime},E^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}=(V^{\prime},E^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> we are given a set <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subseteq V^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subseteq V^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|D|\leq k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|D|\leq k</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\prime}\setminus D\models\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>⊧</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2" title="Lower Bounds ‣ 3 Basic Graphs ‣ On the Descriptive Complexity of Vertex Deletion Problems" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\prime}\setminus D\models\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
1799-For each <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in U</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the copies <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,k+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,k+1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. For every <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\adj u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\adj u</annotation></semantics></math> there is a
1800-triangle <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\adj s\adj s^{\prime}\adj u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∼</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\adj s\adj s^{\prime}\adj u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, but there are no other edges
1801-involving <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, in order to ensure that
1802:<math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"><a href="#S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2" title="Lower Bounds ‣ 3 Basic Graphs ‣ On the Descriptive Complexity of Vertex Deletion Problems" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\ref{lemma:vd-basic-aea}}</annotation></semantics></math> holds, we
1803-either have to (1) delete <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> or (2) delete exactly one of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>
1804-or <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\adj u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\adj u</annotation></semantics></math>. Since there are <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math> copies of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, we
1805-cannot use option (1) for all copies of <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>, so <em id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">for each <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in U</annotation></semantics></math> there must be an <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in S</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\adj u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∼</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">u</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\adj u</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.SS0.SSS0.P0.SPx2.p33.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> or
