+sum(R_1)-sum(R_0) = degree*alpha (mod p). Recover alpha from this invariant,
+choose any b in row 0, and follow b, b+alpha, ... modulo p. At hard (p=113,
+degree=8), two row sums use 14 additions, inversion uses at most 10 Euclidean
+arithmetic steps, and the recurrence uses at most 224 additions/subtractions;
