+    return report
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    print(json.dumps(selftest(), indent=2, sort_keys=True))

codex
The corrected suite has passed through G7; the prior failure was only G8 distinctness because the cheap graph invariant was too coarse on tiny 29-vertex shores. I kept the invariant honest (still explicitly incomplete) and moved the diversity check to the 61-vertex regime, where 20 unrelated generated graphs are distinguished while arbitrary relabelings still collapse.
