codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s Section 3 `aea` Set Cover reduction:

- [gen_2406_18299.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2406.18299/gen_2406_18299.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2406.18299/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2406.18299/README.md)
- [bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2406.18299/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2406.18299/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2406.18299/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local gates pass:

- 0/200,000 structure-aware random guesses.
- Four attacks each failed on 8/8 instances.
- Hopcroft–Karp succeeded on 8/8, honestly reported as the Track B reference algorithm.
- 20/20 canonical-key relabeling and distinctness tests passed.
- Shipping answer: 1,247 characters, 113 atoms.
- Compact affine route: at most 253 arithmetic operations.

The required multi-vendor hardening remains externally blocked: all bare, hinted, and placebo calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” The machine-written error transcripts are retained, but no hardness verdict was fabricated. The family is therefore not ready to submit until `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` has capacity and the three harness arms are rerun.
