    white and with $v_1 \adj v_2$. But now (c) shows that if $v_2 \nadj v_5$, then $v_5$
    is a witness for~$v_2$, allowing us to shorten the walk, because
    the colors of and edges between $v_2$ and $v_5$ are the same as of
    and between $v_4$ and~$v_5$. On the
    other hand, in (d) we see that if $v_2\adj v_5$, then $v_2$ is a 
    witness for~$v_5$, again allowing us to return early, because
    the colors of and edges between $v_5$ and $v_2$ are the same as of
    and between $v_1$ and~$v_2$ (and also of and between $v_3$~and~$v_4$).
